{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-003", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Rising tariffs push footwear margins to a tipping point", "content": "Crocs posted record Q2 2026 revenue of $1.179 billion, with Crocs Brand sales above $1 billion for the first time, but shares fell 7.4 per cent to $123.66.\nTariffs cut adjusted gross margin by 160 basis points, while HEYDUDE wholesale revenue dropped 17.2 per cent to $83 million.\nQ3 adjusted EPS guidance of $3.20-$3.30 trails consensus, signalling tighter footwear sourcing and retail order", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/rising-tariffs-push-footwear-margins-to-a-tipping-point-312296-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-004", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India fixes cotton MSPs; Suvin gets highest support at $103/quintal", "content": "The Government of India has notified MSPs for all Fair Average Quality (FAQ) cotton varieties for the 2026-27 season, with extra-long staple Suvin receiving the highest support price of ₹9,867 per quintal.\nThe Cotton Corporation of India will begin procurement from October 1 if market prices fall below MSP.\nThe schedule also includes quality-linked premiums, deductions, and moisture norms.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-fixes-cotton-msps-suvin-gets-highest-support-at-103-quintal-312295-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-005", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indian polyester market sees mixed feedstock trends as Hormuz risk", "content": "Indian polyester raw material prices were mixed in the week ended August 1, with PTA softer, MEG firmer and melt costs higher. \nFilament yarn makers raised POY and PTY prices, while PSF stayed unchanged, shaping purchase decisions for mills and sourcing teams.\nNear-term polyester prices will track crude oil, feedstock markets and any renewed Strait of Hormuz disruption. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indian-polyester-market-sees-mixed-feedstock-trends-as-hormuz-risk-312289-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-006", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Foreign firms grab 80% of Bangladesh’s freight earnings: CSR study", "content": "Foreign-owned shipping firms grab about 80 per cent of Bangladesh’s annual freight earnings, while domestic-flagged ocean vessels get only 8-10 per cent, a study found. \nRaising the number of Bangladesh-flagged vessels by 20 per cent could help retain up to $2 billion within the country, it noted. \nA lawmaker said foreign ownership in the sector should not reach 40 per cent that poses security risks. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/foreign-firms-grab-80-of-bangladesh-s-freight-earnings-csr-study-312288-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-007", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "SMEs face hurdles limiting ability to be energy-efficient: IEA article", "content": "As SMEs are often among the least equipped to manage price shocks arising out of successive energy crises, improving energy efficiency offers them a way to reduce bills and emissions, raise profits, strengthen resilience to future price shocks and enhance competitiveness, IEA analysts say. \nHowever, SMEs face structural barriers that limit their ability to invest in energy‑efficient solutions, they note. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/smes-face-hurdles-limiting-ability-to-be-energy-efficient-iea-article-312279-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-008", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India’s Raymond Lifestyle’s Q1 earnings grow 11%; garmenting jumps 50%", "content": "Raymond Lifestyle has reported a stable Q1 FY27, with total income rising 6 per cent YoY to ₹1,560 crore (~$163.7 million) and EBITDA up 11 per cent to ₹135 crore (~$14.17 million). \nStrong garmenting growth, driven by export demand and trade tailwinds, offset softer textile performance. \nThe company also strengthened its balance sheet, ending the quarter with a net cash position. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-s-raymond-lifestyle-s-q1-earnings-grow-11-garmenting-jumps-50--312300-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-009", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh can unlock $5 bn apparel exports with plastic recycling", "content": "Bangladesh could add $4-5 billion in apparel exports by scaling plastic-to-textile recycling, BUILD has estimated. \nThe push targets lower reliance on imported man-made fibres and alignment with European Union's circularity requirements. \nPolicy proposals include a circular economy policy, better collection, traceability, recycled PET standards and certification. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-can-unlock-5-bn-apparel-exports-with-plastic-recycling-312290-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
